<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιάζω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>CG</u>
			2
		</span></i> (v.l.): fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.42
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμφίασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.368
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Eryc.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				200.24
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Axum</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				1.27.2
			</span></i> (v.l.), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Her.Prooem.</u>
				2
			</span></i>: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμφίακα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συν-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Clearch.
				25
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άσομαι </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				86
			</span></i> codd.: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμφιασάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.
					2.1.2
				</span></i>
			, etc.: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμφίασμαι</span> in med. sense (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				16.11
			</span></i> (v.l.):— <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιέζω</span>
			is a common v.l.: (perh. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφί,</span> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάζω</span> from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί</span>):— later word
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιέννυμι,</span>
			<i>ciothe,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span> Plu.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱματίοις τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.: metaph., of the grave, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέα
				ἠμφίασεν</span>
			<u>AP</u>l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίαν ἀσαφείᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					20.235a
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>put on,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιάσασθαί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Jb.</u>
					40.10
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i> l. c.</div>
